    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0946" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg876"/>

                <head>No. 564.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 9,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 245, of the 12th ultimo, in
                    relation to the revision of the Turkish tariff and our treaty of 1862 with that
                    Government, has been received, and your note to the minister for foreign affairs
                    upon the subject meets with the Department’s approval. While we are satisfied
                    that under the strict engagements of the treaty the fourth period of seven years
                    has already begun to run, we are not averse to making such revision as is
                    suggested in the concluding part of your note, and bringing our tariff
                    engagements with Turkey into harmony with her like engagements with other powers
                    before the end of the now current period of seven years.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
